WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:00.001 --> 00:00.992
(All characters, locations, and events are fictional

4
00:01.017 --> 00:02.038
and for entertainment purposes only.

5
00:02.063 --> 00:03.107
No actions depicted are intended to be encouraged or endorsed.

6
00:03.132 --> 00:03.994
Animals were specially trained and supervised by professionals.

7
00:04.019 --> 00:04.936
Viewer discretion is advised.)

8
00:05.724 --> 00:08.504
Golf may not be a game for the most skilled.

9
00:08.529 --> 00:10.984
But it is a game for those who never give up.

10
00:11.009 --> 00:13.638
We may miss a shot or hit the ball out of the fairway,

11
00:13.663 --> 00:15.798
but we never run from the obstacles ahead.

12
00:17.150 --> 00:20.365
Life is the same. No one wins every hole.

13
00:20.390 --> 00:22.663
But the strongest among us

14
00:22.688 --> 00:25.180
are those who dare to face their own mistakes

15
00:25.205 --> 00:27.770
and find a new way to deal with them without hesitation.

16
00:27.795 --> 00:29.021
Love is the same.

17
00:29.046 --> 00:30.593
If you're afraid of making a mistake,

18
00:30.618 --> 00:32.393
you'll never truly play the game.

19
00:32.449 --> 00:34.607
We have to dare to take the shot, dare to take risks.

20
00:34.632 --> 00:36.160
and dare to face the consequences,

21
00:36.185 --> 00:38.185
whatever the outcome may be.

22
00:38.497 --> 00:41.769
Many think golf is all about distance.

23
00:41.794 --> 00:44.654
But golf isn't a sport won by sheer power.

24
00:44.679 --> 00:47.179
It's about learning to control your own heart.

25
00:47.204 --> 00:50.539
Because on the course, no one is fighting us but ourselves.

26
00:50.564 --> 00:52.204
Every hole is a question.

27
00:52.229 --> 00:53.949
Every swing is an answer.

28
00:53.996 --> 00:56.952
Because a true golfer doesn't win by hitting the best shots,

29
00:56.977 --> 00:59.317
but by refusing to give up on themselves.

30
01:02.163 --> 01:04.888
(Pro Kaimook - Thidapa Kitjakarn)

31
01:10.759 --> 01:14.280
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

32
01:14.915 --> 01:16.576
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

33
01:16.608 --> 01:20.245
♪ It's plain to see ♪

34
01:20.270 --> 01:22.397
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

35
01:22.439 --> 01:25.759
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

36
01:26.532 --> 01:28.215
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

37
01:28.240 --> 01:31.805
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

38
01:32.020 --> 01:34.020
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

39
01:34.045 --> 01:36.922
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

40
01:36.947 --> 01:38.781
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

41
01:38.806 --> 01:41.657
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

42
01:41.682 --> 01:44.511
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

43
01:44.536 --> 01:48.394
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

44
01:48.419 --> 01:50.439
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

45
01:50.464 --> 01:53.305
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

46
01:53.330 --> 01:56.703
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

47
01:56.728 --> 02:01.479
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

48
02:01.504 --> 02:03.554
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

49
02:04.904 --> 02:07.007
Thank you all so, so much.

50
02:07.032 --> 02:09.899
None of this would've turned out this well without all of you.

51
02:09.924 --> 02:11.440
Allez, allez!

52
02:11.465 --> 02:13.465
- Allez, allez! - Allez, allez!

53
02:13.490 --> 02:16.795
- Allez, allez! - Allez, allez!

54
02:16.827 --> 02:19.843
Nana, are you okay?

55
02:19.876 --> 02:21.555
- Allez, allez! - Allez, allez!

56
02:21.580 --> 02:23.381
Oh, Miss Nana!

57
02:23.406 --> 02:25.850
The doctor said you probably haven't been getting enough rest.

58
02:25.875 --> 02:27.235
and are just feeling fatigued.

59
02:27.918 --> 02:30.102
- Oh, Mr. Sanchai. - Hello, Doctor.

60
02:30.417 --> 02:32.406
About your chemotherapy treatment plan...

61
02:32.431 --> 02:34.726
Have you decided when you'd like to start?

62
02:58.198 --> 02:59.357
You're awake?

63
03:00.055 --> 03:01.587
Is it morning already, Vee?

64
03:06.084 --> 03:08.540
- About last night... - Oh!

65
03:09.684 --> 03:12.027
Let's not talk about last night.

66
03:15.983 --> 03:19.686
It'd be nice to wake up next to you every morning, Vee.

67
03:21.039 --> 03:22.310
You'd really want that?

68
03:22.834 --> 03:24.016
Why not?

69
03:27.523 --> 03:29.968
We don't have to wake up next to each other every morning.

70
03:29.993 --> 03:32.660
Wouldn't it be better if we had each other every day?

71
03:44.833 --> 03:46.701
What are you doing, Vee?

72
03:46.726 --> 03:49.297
The sun's in my eyes. It's hurting.

73
03:50.915 --> 03:52.389
I'm going to take a shower.

74
03:53.326 --> 03:55.612
- I'm not letting you go. - Vee!

75
03:56.523 --> 03:59.975
What are you doing, Vee?

76
04:00.150 --> 04:02.460
- Take that! - That tickles!

77
04:05.203 --> 04:07.778
- I'm hungry. - What do you want to eat?

78
04:07.803 --> 04:09.951
- Anything's fine. - Good morning, Nana. Pro Vee.

79
04:09.976 --> 04:11.318
- Morning. - Morning.

80
04:11.343 --> 04:12.780
Hi, Nana.

81
04:13.535 --> 04:15.870
Oh, Fahsai.

82
04:16.258 --> 04:17.768
Good morning, Pro Vee.

83
04:18.206 --> 04:19.477
What a coincidence.

84
04:19.502 --> 04:21.502
I just went by the clubhouse,

85
04:21.527 --> 04:23.251
and they said you might be at the office.

86
04:23.683 --> 04:26.310
Oh, do you have a lesson today, Fahsai?

87
04:27.421 --> 04:30.064
No, but I'm free today,

88
04:30.089 --> 04:31.920
so I thought I'd drop by.

89
04:31.945 --> 04:34.311
But I checked your schedule,

90
04:34.336 --> 04:36.336
and you're free today.

91
04:39.282 --> 04:41.675
You're free today, Pro Vee?

92
04:44.625 --> 04:46.625
Uh...

93
04:48.314 --> 04:49.763
- I'm not. - What?

94
04:49.788 --> 04:53.433
But the staff at the course said you were free until this evening.

95
04:53.863 --> 04:55.444
- I'm not. - Pro Vee...

96
04:55.469 --> 04:58.516
Pro Vee must have a meeting about...

97
05:00.313 --> 05:04.655
Um, choosing a new type of grass to test on the course.

98
05:05.235 --> 05:07.050
A meeting that lasts all afternoon?

99
05:07.963 --> 05:09.479
Mm-hmm. That's right.

100
05:09.614 --> 05:12.860
- Just about the grass? - Mm-hmm.

101
05:14.969 --> 05:16.393
That's too bad.

102
05:17.708 --> 05:18.816
Are you free tomorrow then?

103
05:18.841 --> 05:21.064
You probably don't remember your own schedule.

104
05:21.089 --> 05:22.978
I'll check the system for you.

105
05:25.270 --> 05:26.997
Tomorrow... booked.

106
05:27.162 --> 05:28.793
The day after... booked.

107
05:28.968 --> 05:32.723
And the days after that... booked, booked, booked.

108
05:33.218 --> 05:34.808
Sorry, Fahsai.

109
05:34.833 --> 05:37.643
Pro Vee's schedule is packed until...

110
05:37.668 --> 05:38.850
the end of the month.

111
05:38.953 --> 05:40.369
That busy?

112
05:41.274 --> 05:42.274
Yep.

113
05:43.307 --> 05:44.798
If you want to improve your swing,

114
05:44.823 --> 05:46.502
I can recommend another pro.

115
05:46.526 --> 05:48.194
They're just as good. Want me to?

116
05:49.258 --> 05:52.262
No, I don't want to change pros.

117
05:52.533 --> 05:54.962
Sorry, Fahsai.

118
05:54.987 --> 05:57.743
Vee and I have another meeting. We should go.

119
05:57.768 --> 05:59.825
Oh, wait, wait, wait!

120
05:59.866 --> 06:00.897
Here.

121
06:01.318 --> 06:04.338
I got something for Pro Vee, too.

122
06:04.553 --> 06:07.770
It's a handcrafted grey sedge handbag from Phatthalung.

123
06:08.009 --> 06:09.826
- Thank you. - Can you take a picture of me?

124
06:10.924 --> 06:11.965
Sure.

125
06:13.920 --> 06:16.828
One, two, three... Beautiful!

126
06:16.868 --> 06:19.615
Mm, you look so cute, Pro Vee. That's a wrap.

127
06:23.115 --> 06:25.613
We'll get going. We're gonna be late. Come on.

128
06:27.854 --> 06:30.372
You're really wicked, Nana.

129
06:30.747 --> 06:32.860
I can be much worse,

130
06:32.885 --> 06:34.656
if she weren't my friend.

131
06:51.058 --> 06:54.335
On behalf of Goodview Golf Club, I'd like to thank you all

132
06:54.360 --> 06:58.187
for choosing us to host today's Golf Course Network meeting.

133
07:00.245 --> 07:02.726
Before we begin the meeting at 1 PM,

134
07:02.751 --> 07:06.315
we'd like to welcome you all with a special lunch.

135
07:06.871 --> 07:09.272
That's wonderful. I've heard for a while

136
07:09.748 --> 07:11.804
that everything here is delicious.

137
07:12.654 --> 07:13.683
Isn't that right, Nut?

138
07:13.993 --> 07:15.000
It is.

139
07:15.818 --> 07:17.924
And what if we fall in love with it?

140
07:19.701 --> 07:22.778
We might have to steal the chef, or maybe buy the whole course.

141
07:25.573 --> 07:27.102
I don't think it'll come to that.

142
07:27.427 --> 07:29.427
Our course offers delivery.

143
07:29.619 --> 07:32.154
If you can't make it here, you can always order in.

144
07:33.282 --> 07:34.467
That's great.

145
07:34.492 --> 07:36.727
I think my course needs something like that.

146
07:37.241 --> 07:38.343
You're more than welcome.

147
07:38.368 --> 07:39.810
If there's something that works well,

148
07:39.834 --> 07:41.561
feel free to adapt it for your own course.

149
07:41.586 --> 07:42.989
I don't mind sharing.

150
07:43.530 --> 07:44.725
How generous of you.

151
07:45.209 --> 07:47.209
Yes. If I weren't so generous,

152
07:47.234 --> 07:52.680
you wouldn't be sitting right here with us today.

153
08:01.486 --> 08:03.743
Greetings, esteemed guests!

154
08:03.768 --> 08:07.078
Chef Queen here. Your lunch is ready!

155
08:07.275 --> 08:10.234
Our course offers a wide variety of international cuisine,

156
08:10.259 --> 08:13.562
including French cuisine,

157
08:18.611 --> 08:20.848
and all four regions of Thai cuisine.

158
08:21.126 --> 08:23.126
Feel all the feeling.

159
08:58.098 --> 09:00.389
Please enjoy!

160
09:00.414 --> 09:02.279
- Please, help yourselves. - Enjoy, everyone.

161
09:10.856 --> 09:13.151
The main agenda for today is

162
09:13.176 --> 09:17.089
the All Star Women's Golf Tournament.

163
09:17.477 --> 09:20.164
Women's golf is gaining popularity in our country.

164
09:20.189 --> 09:23.317
I believe we should seize this opportunity

165
09:23.342 --> 09:26.192
to support and promote the sport,

166
09:26.217 --> 09:28.553
and help make golf more widespread.

167
09:28.578 --> 09:30.001
And in the future,

168
09:30.026 --> 09:34.623
we could also organize events for children, youth, and seniors.

169
09:34.786 --> 09:38.452
Each course will send one representative

170
09:38.477 --> 09:40.205
to compete in the tournament.

171
09:40.230 --> 09:43.776
And whichever course's player wins will represent us

172
09:43.801 --> 09:48.265
in the Asian Tour taking place later this year.

173
09:49.733 --> 09:52.166
What course will host the tournament?

174
09:52.191 --> 09:54.124
If we're looking for the biggest course,

175
09:54.149 --> 09:55.995
wouldn't that be Siam Green Golf?

176
09:56.201 --> 09:57.480
I'm afraid not.

177
09:57.505 --> 09:59.977
We're currently undergoing a major renovation.

178
10:00.699 --> 10:03.081
The Royal Green is available. We're ready to host.

179
10:04.051 --> 10:06.688
But the course hosting the tournament

180
10:06.713 --> 10:10.581
also needs to have a hotel or accommodations for the golfers.

181
10:10.606 --> 10:11.838
That's true.

182
10:11.863 --> 10:14.413
Especially for players coming from other provinces,

183
10:14.438 --> 10:17.207
and the media coming to cover the event.

184
10:17.661 --> 10:19.535
There's a hotel near our course.

185
10:19.560 --> 10:21.323
It's only a little over ten kilometers away.

186
10:21.348 --> 10:23.093
I'd call that pretty far.

187
10:25.519 --> 10:28.783
In that case, Goodview could be another option.

188
10:29.510 --> 10:31.763
Our hotel was just renovated,

189
10:32.216 --> 10:34.224
and I'm confident it can accommodate everyone.

190
10:34.249 --> 10:37.602
And the hotel is less than a kilometer from the course.

191
10:44.083 --> 10:45.143
That sounds good.

192
10:45.683 --> 10:48.971
The course is spacious and has all the necessary facilities.

193
10:51.550 --> 10:52.794
Then it's settled.

194
10:52.819 --> 10:55.373
I think this would be the most suitable venue.

195
11:09.498 --> 11:12.281
I'll work out the details for the tournament preparations

196
11:12.306 --> 11:14.523
and present the plan in two days.

197
11:15.269 --> 11:16.618
Thank you, Nut.

198
11:17.445 --> 11:20.147
So, Nana, who will you send to represent our course?

199
11:25.129 --> 11:28.140
Represent us? What do you mean?

200
11:28.608 --> 11:31.023
The Golf Course Network is organizing a tournament...

201
11:31.974 --> 11:35.122
Ms. Nana, it's bad. Something big has happened.

202
11:37.034 --> 11:39.034
The wastewater is this close?

203
11:39.344 --> 11:41.729
How are we supposed to eat with this right here?

204
11:41.754 --> 11:42.777
Where are they?

205
11:44.914 --> 11:47.707
No one's taking responsibility. No one's doing anything about it.

206
11:47.732 --> 11:50.298
- How are you going to fix this? - The villagers are suffering.

207
11:50.323 --> 11:52.443
- Everyone, everyone! - This isn't right.

208
11:52.468 --> 11:54.062
Please, everyone, calm down.

209
11:54.298 --> 11:56.273
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

210
11:56.368 --> 11:58.866
Misunderstood what? It's right in front of us, isn't it?

211
11:58.891 --> 11:59.953
- Yeah. - Yeah.

212
11:59.978 --> 12:03.019
The water reeks, and look at all the dead fish floating around.

213
12:03.044 --> 12:05.673
It stinks everywhere. How are we supposed to live like this?

214
12:06.888 --> 12:09.016
You keep the nice, clean places for yourselves,

215
12:09.041 --> 12:10.858
and dump all the filthy stuff on us.

216
12:10.883 --> 12:13.210
That's selfish, you hear me?

217
12:13.235 --> 12:14.241
Am I right, everyone?

218
12:14.266 --> 12:16.934
- That's right! Selfish! - Selfish!

219
12:16.959 --> 12:20.890
If this is how it's going to be, we can't live together anymore.

220
12:20.915 --> 12:22.577
We won't stand for this. No way!

221
12:22.602 --> 12:24.299
Right, everyone?

222
12:24.324 --> 12:26.031
- Let's talk this out. - Then what are you gonna do?

223
12:26.056 --> 12:27.896
We can't even eat or drink properly anymore.

224
12:27.921 --> 12:29.626
Everyone, please, hear me out.

225
12:31.304 --> 12:33.276
As the owner of this place,

226
12:33.301 --> 12:36.111
I'm sorry to hear about the trouble you're going through.

227
12:36.136 --> 12:39.074
But could you give me some time to look into the facts first?

228
12:39.272 --> 12:41.272
Are you trying to shirk responsibility?

229
12:41.909 --> 12:44.287
We've heard people say that so many times before.

230
12:44.312 --> 12:45.947
And in the end, nothing ever happens.

231
12:46.130 --> 12:47.285
That's not what I'm doing.

232
12:47.310 --> 12:49.165
Our golf course has been part of this community

233
12:49.189 --> 12:51.032
since my grandfather's time.

234
12:51.205 --> 12:53.890
We've never had anything like this happen before, have we?

235
12:55.150 --> 12:57.770
If the wastewater is coming from our course,

236
12:57.795 --> 12:59.167
I'll take responsibility.

237
12:59.562 --> 13:01.030
How will you take responsibility?

238
13:01.175 --> 13:04.339
I'll do whatever it takes to restore the water source

239
13:04.364 --> 13:06.823
and improve the environment for everyone in the community.

240
13:07.058 --> 13:08.401
But how can we trust you?

241
13:08.426 --> 13:10.426
Exactly. What do we do, everyone?

242
13:10.563 --> 13:12.682
- We can't live with that stench! - It's awful!

243
13:12.707 --> 13:14.446
- The fish are dead! - They can't handle it.

244
13:14.471 --> 13:15.605
Hear her out first.

245
13:17.174 --> 13:22.111
All right, then. We'll give you three more days.

246
13:22.971 --> 13:24.518
Then we'll come back for an answer.

247
13:37.138 --> 13:39.876
I'm sure the wastewater didn't come from our course.

248
13:40.193 --> 13:43.063
We had the treatment system inspected just last week.

249
13:43.088 --> 13:44.357
Everything was fine.

250
13:44.830 --> 13:48.014
The chemicals can't reach the community water source.

251
13:48.498 --> 13:50.261
We only have three days.

252
13:50.429 --> 13:52.034
Where should we start?

253
13:52.201 --> 13:53.946
We need to find evidence

254
13:53.970 --> 13:56.560
to prove our innocence and win the villagers back.

255
13:57.782 --> 14:00.119
Should we collect water samples and have them tested?

256
14:00.144 --> 14:01.181
Good idea.

257
14:01.206 --> 14:04.451
That could be the evidence we need to prove we're innocent.

258
14:04.713 --> 14:07.369
Miss Nana, there's a problem!

259
14:07.837 --> 14:10.037
Perfect. You're all here. Let's figure it out together.

260
14:10.062 --> 14:14.239
Someone posted that they ordered delivery from our course,

261
14:14.264 --> 14:16.369
but the food arrived spoiled.

262
14:16.393 --> 14:18.640
Here's another one. This person says

263
14:18.665 --> 14:21.381
they ordered our food, then got food poisoning.

264
14:21.406 --> 14:22.708
This is really bad.

265
14:22.732 --> 14:24.524
It hurts our rating. They gave us one star.

266
14:24.549 --> 14:25.862
And here's another one.

267
14:25.887 --> 14:28.791
They say they ordered our food, but never received it,

268
14:28.816 --> 14:30.732
yet they were still charged through the app.

269
14:30.757 --> 14:32.376
But is any of this true, Chef Queen?

270
14:33.598 --> 14:35.854
I think someone's trying to sabotage us.

271
14:35.879 --> 14:38.029
Why do you think someone's sabotaging us?

272
14:38.521 --> 14:42.000
Miss Nana, I've been cooking for over 20 years.

273
14:42.025 --> 14:45.184
When it comes to food quality, I check every dish that goes out.

274
14:45.209 --> 14:47.669
And as for delivery, I don't think we could've messed up.

275
14:47.694 --> 14:50.163
We've practiced it so many times. No way.

276
14:53.142 --> 14:56.124
Looks like all the posts came from the same email address.

277
14:56.149 --> 14:57.357
They just changed the names.

278
15:18.292 --> 15:19.317
Want a drink?

279
15:19.976 --> 15:20.991
What?

280
15:21.452 --> 15:23.238
A student at the course brought it as a gift.

281
15:23.477 --> 15:25.057
Plum wine from Phrae.

282
15:26.486 --> 15:27.487
Want to try it?

283
15:27.955 --> 15:30.288
Just one glass. I've still got work to finish.

284
15:34.787 --> 15:38.445
I heard things got pretty hectic at the course today.

285
15:39.058 --> 15:41.927
That's why I'm still working this late.

286
15:49.567 --> 15:52.587
Why does everything always end up on your plate?

287
15:53.414 --> 15:56.339
I guess I'm the most efficient person at the course.

288
15:58.177 --> 15:59.471
Proud of yourself?

289
15:59.683 --> 16:02.754
Of course. Whenever there was a problem,

290
16:03.088 --> 16:04.738
Mr. Sanchai would send me in.

291
16:05.045 --> 16:08.687
Just like now, when I'm Nana's right-hand woman.

292
16:11.165 --> 16:14.240
Why doesn't Miss Nana find another left hand?

293
16:14.741 --> 16:17.617
Then her right hand could have some private time.

294
16:24.060 --> 16:25.740
Can I help you with anything?

295
16:26.273 --> 16:27.375
I've got a free hand.

296
16:28.137 --> 16:29.312
I'm fine.

297
16:31.951 --> 16:35.883
So Jinny's hand right here

298
16:36.502 --> 16:38.718
can't help Miss right hand at all?

299
17:02.668 --> 17:04.129
Is this better?

300
17:06.462 --> 17:07.774
Thank you.

301
17:12.346 --> 17:14.678
Starting to see the benefits of my hand, huh?

302
17:21.955 --> 17:23.160
What do you want?

303
17:24.953 --> 17:27.574
Just checking on you.

304
17:32.307 --> 17:34.167
Don't beat around the bush.

305
17:34.192 --> 17:36.064
I still have a lot of work to finish.

306
20:57.752 --> 21:00.452
But the canal water really does smell bad, Nut.

307
21:00.715 --> 21:02.460
Mm. It really does.

308
21:02.874 --> 21:05.376
But the smell isn't coming from the water, Nana.

309
21:05.401 --> 21:06.773
What do you mean?

310
21:06.965 --> 21:09.222
It's coming from around the canal.

311
21:09.619 --> 21:11.678
Then what about all those dead fish?

312
21:11.703 --> 21:12.844
There were so many of them.

313
21:12.930 --> 21:14.824
That almost made it convincing, too.

314
21:14.849 --> 21:17.420
But the fish that washed up dead are marine fish,

315
21:17.609 --> 21:19.043
not freshwater fish.

316
21:19.068 --> 21:21.455
So the samples you had Belle send for testing,

317
21:21.700 --> 21:23.849
the water and the dead fish...

318
21:23.874 --> 21:28.566
Exactly. The test results will prove our course is innocent.

319
21:29.811 --> 21:33.435
Are you saying our course is being framed?

320
21:36.567 --> 21:39.657
Then who's behind it? And why would they do this?

321
21:47.842 --> 21:49.241
Everyone! Manager!

322
21:49.266 --> 21:51.665
The packaging is definitely from our course.

323
21:51.690 --> 21:52.942
It's from my restaurant,

324
21:52.967 --> 21:55.548
but I didn't make the food inside.

325
21:55.573 --> 21:58.685
It's not ours. Look at the basil.

326
21:58.710 --> 22:00.846
That's not how I cut my squid.

327
22:04.402 --> 22:07.116
I don't know who messed up,

328
22:07.141 --> 22:10.428
but it didn't sit right with me, so I called to check.

329
22:10.453 --> 22:12.534
I asked whether anyone had placed an order

330
22:12.559 --> 22:14.443
around the same time they posted those reviews.

331
22:14.468 --> 22:17.729
But no one had even ordered any of those dishes.

332
22:18.499 --> 22:20.209
Chef Queen, do you suspect anyone?

333
22:22.122 --> 22:23.618
Could it be March?

334
22:25.455 --> 22:27.836
Ms. Yupadee from The Royal Green.

335
22:30.128 --> 22:32.859
I'm not trying to accuse anyone,

336
22:32.884 --> 22:35.764
but Pro Jin once told me

337
22:35.789 --> 22:38.651
she'd seen Pro Vee at Ms. Yupadee's course.

338
22:40.231 --> 22:41.646
Pro Vee?

339
22:41.670 --> 22:44.894
No way. Pro Vee would never do that.

340
22:45.077 --> 22:46.569
If anyone's suspicious,

341
22:46.594 --> 22:48.340
it's Pro Jin.

342
22:48.570 --> 22:50.249
She used to work at that course.

343
22:50.274 --> 22:52.741
She could've come here to get information about our course

344
22:52.766 --> 22:54.520
and pass it on to them.

345
23:04.662 --> 23:07.109
I didn't think you'd take it this far.

346
23:07.134 --> 23:08.371
You've got some nerve.

347
23:10.702 --> 23:12.438
I told you.

348
23:12.463 --> 23:15.692
If I'm going to do something, I'm going all the way.

349
23:17.002 --> 23:20.550
That's how you play the game in business.

350
23:21.296 --> 23:23.026
The weak lose.

351
23:23.818 --> 23:27.856
Only the strong get to have it all.

352
23:29.818 --> 23:32.156
With results like these,

353
23:33.124 --> 23:34.870
don't I deserve a little bonus?

354
23:50.465 --> 23:52.321
- Pro Vee. - Hmm?

355
23:52.488 --> 23:54.345
There's something I want to ask you.

356
23:55.417 --> 23:56.466
What is it?

357
24:00.259 --> 24:03.623
You know our course is being sabotaged, right?

358
24:04.130 --> 24:07.216
Mm. I've heard about it from some of the staff.

359
24:07.352 --> 24:08.765
Is there anything I can help with?

360
24:22.421 --> 24:27.077
Someone said they saw you at The Royal Green.

361
24:27.599 --> 24:29.217
- So I wanted to... - Yes.

362
24:29.242 --> 24:31.805
Ms. Yupadee, the owner, asked me to meet with her.

363
24:33.166 --> 24:35.860
Can I ask what you talked about?

364
24:37.208 --> 24:39.452
She asked me to teach at her course.

365
24:39.509 --> 24:42.183
She even offered to pay me more.

366
24:44.758 --> 24:47.013
Oh. I see.

367
24:50.053 --> 24:51.424
Is something wrong?

368
24:54.831 --> 24:57.564
People at the course think

369
24:57.589 --> 25:00.645
The Royal Green is behind all of this

370
25:00.805 --> 25:03.038
to discredit our course.

371
25:03.063 --> 25:06.533
So they think I might be involved.

372
25:07.958 --> 25:09.212
That's not true.

373
25:09.585 --> 25:12.681
- We're trying to find out... - Do you think I am?

374
25:21.150 --> 25:23.425
If it wasn't Pro Vee, who else do you think it could be?

375
25:23.450 --> 25:25.450
- Pro Jin. - Are you crazy?

376
25:27.366 --> 25:29.114
You used to work there.

377
25:29.139 --> 25:31.306
And when I asked you to join this course,

378
25:31.331 --> 25:33.054
you moved here right away.

379
25:33.987 --> 25:35.738
I may look cold and intimidating,

380
25:35.763 --> 25:38.353
but I would never do something that ridiculous.

381
25:38.378 --> 25:41.317
And I hate people who play dirty.

382
25:41.342 --> 25:43.753
What do you mean by "play dirty"?

383
25:44.859 --> 25:47.028
Your boss's favorite pro.

384
25:47.053 --> 25:48.427
She may have a pretty face,

385
25:48.452 --> 25:50.660
but who would've thought she'd do something like that?

386
25:50.685 --> 25:53.457
Do something like what? What exactly do you mean?

387
25:53.691 --> 25:55.316
What? Tell me.

388
25:57.734 --> 26:00.654
Wait, Vee. That's not what I meant.

389
26:00.776 --> 26:01.871
It's not like that.

390
26:01.896 --> 26:03.252
I was just telling you...

391
26:03.277 --> 26:04.498
But the reason you told me

392
26:05.098 --> 26:06.908
because you wanted to know

393
26:06.933 --> 26:08.488
if I did it, didn't you?

394
26:09.219 --> 26:10.854
That's not what I meant.

395
26:11.189 --> 26:12.708
I really didn't think that.

396
26:12.733 --> 26:14.607
I'll sleep in my own room tonight.

397
26:15.027 --> 26:16.083
Otherwise,

398
26:16.965 --> 26:18.524
you might not trust me.

399
26:18.628 --> 26:22.421
No, that's not it. Please, believe me.

400
26:22.446 --> 26:24.261
I really didn't think that.

401
26:27.359 --> 26:29.979
I never thought you'd do something like that, Vee.

402
26:30.630 --> 26:32.050
Belle told me

403
26:32.075 --> 26:35.444
that Pro Jin saw you at that course,

404
26:35.469 --> 26:39.909
so everyone started putting the pieces together...

405
26:45.175 --> 26:48.293
Then why did you and Pro Vee have the same coach back then?

406
26:48.825 --> 26:50.983
It's not complicated. I couldn't afford one.

407
26:51.886 --> 26:54.277
My family didn't really support me playing golf.

408
26:54.467 --> 26:57.540
Vee knew that, so she offered to share her coach with me.

409
26:57.834 --> 26:59.788
Just having Pro Vee's coach come over

410
26:59.813 --> 27:01.653
and coach you during the match

411
27:01.678 --> 27:03.149
was enough to get you disqualified?

412
27:03.174 --> 27:06.392
According to the rules, a golfer can't receive advice from anyone

413
27:06.417 --> 27:08.012
other than their own caddie.

414
27:08.403 --> 27:10.823
If someone tells them the line, how to hit the shot,

415
27:10.848 --> 27:12.390
or interferes with their decisions,

416
27:12.414 --> 27:15.027
the golfer is penalized immediately.

417
27:15.290 --> 27:17.387
But why would the coach do that

418
27:17.412 --> 27:19.230
when he knew the rules so well?

419
27:20.192 --> 27:22.751
Exactly. What else am I supposed to think?

420
27:23.330 --> 27:26.552
And Venus won that match just like she wanted.

421
27:29.051 --> 27:32.205
What if the coach did it without Pro Vee knowing?

422
27:34.086 --> 27:35.396
Don't be so naive.

423
27:36.017 --> 27:38.542
He must've known that if I made it to the final hole,

424
27:38.828 --> 27:40.352
I'd definitely have the highest score.

425
27:41.638 --> 27:46.446
So you think Pro Vee was involved in discrediting our course.

426
27:46.822 --> 27:48.903
Someone who's done something like that before

427
27:48.928 --> 27:50.476
could certainly do it again.

428
27:51.717 --> 27:54.844
She might've even taken a big payout from them.

429
28:06.303 --> 28:08.287
I'm sorry, Vee.

430
28:18.924 --> 28:22.278
Don't cry. I believe you now. I believe you.

431
28:28.932 --> 28:30.747
It's okay. Don't cry.

432
28:44.355 --> 28:46.433
Let me tell you this, Nana.

433
28:46.822 --> 28:50.553
If there's anyone in this world who wants the best for you,

434
28:51.089 --> 28:52.821
I'll always be one of them.

435
28:55.646 --> 28:57.052
I know.

436
28:57.866 --> 29:01.884
I told everyone that you'd never do something like that.

437
29:02.189 --> 29:03.637
If anyone's suspicious,

438
29:03.662 --> 29:05.215
it's Pro Jin.

439
29:05.240 --> 29:08.685
No, don't. Don't accuse people like that without proof.

440
29:11.910 --> 29:15.058
Nut said the evidence has already been sent for testing.

441
29:15.083 --> 29:18.180
We'll know the truth soon, okay?

442
29:21.101 --> 29:23.821
Come on, don't cry.

443
29:23.846 --> 29:25.846
You're an executive now.

444
29:26.028 --> 29:28.485
How can you sit here crying your eyes out like this?

445
29:28.835 --> 29:30.835
You'll lose all your credibility.

446
29:34.812 --> 29:38.049
Don't cry. Come here.

447
29:42.625 --> 29:43.882
That's enough now.

448
33:17.775 --> 33:20.019
As I promised everyone,

449
33:20.044 --> 33:22.576
we've looked into the wastewater in the community

450
33:22.601 --> 33:24.508
to find out what caused it.

451
33:24.533 --> 33:27.218
But first, I'd like to explain

452
33:27.243 --> 33:29.329
that our course has a wastewater treatment system

453
33:29.354 --> 33:31.380
before any water is discharged into the waterway.

454
33:31.405 --> 33:33.485
We also carefully select our fertilizers and other chemicals.

455
33:33.510 --> 33:36.113
We only use environmentally friendly products.

456
33:38.441 --> 33:39.552
Environmentally friendly?

457
33:39.955 --> 33:41.678
Then how do you explain all those dead fish?

458
33:41.703 --> 33:43.035
Yeah, exactly.

459
33:43.575 --> 33:46.504
The dead fish in the water weren't native fish.

460
33:46.529 --> 33:49.686
They were marine fish planted there to stage the scene.

461
33:49.711 --> 33:51.575
As for the smell,

462
33:51.750 --> 33:54.064
someone poured chemicals around the area.

463
33:54.089 --> 33:57.302
They don't harm the waterway. They only cause a bad smell.

464
33:57.770 --> 34:01.697
Today, I have invited experts from the relevant authorities

465
34:01.722 --> 34:03.722
to explain everything to everyone.

466
34:04.193 --> 34:05.232
Please, go ahead.

467
34:10.761 --> 34:12.358
As you can see,

468
34:12.383 --> 34:14.801
this is a water sample taken from the community canal,

469
34:14.841 --> 34:16.615
and this is a sample from the holding pond

470
34:16.640 --> 34:18.215
where the course discharges its water.

471
34:18.239 --> 34:21.662
Our tests found that the community's water

472
34:21.687 --> 34:23.687
has a COD, or Chemical Oxygen...

473
34:51.490 --> 34:53.829
I actually know a thing or two about hotel operations.

474
34:54.881 --> 34:57.444
Maybe next time I could help you with your work in Chiang Rai?

475
34:57.603 --> 34:59.603
Let's save this course first.

476
34:59.994 --> 35:03.990
So, who are you sending to represent our course

477
35:04.015 --> 35:06.015
in the All Star Women's Golf Tournament?

478
35:06.269 --> 35:07.590
I've already got a plan.

479
35:08.415 --> 35:10.789
Our course is definitely taking home the championship.

480
35:12.507 --> 35:13.686
Don't get ahead of yourself.

481
35:16.751 --> 35:18.466
If something goes wrong,

482
35:18.491 --> 35:20.777
I don't want to hear your excuses afterward.

483
35:41.971 --> 35:43.343
Who should I put up against her?

484
35:45.018 --> 35:46.438
The pros here are all lousy.

485
36:02.075 --> 36:03.420
Don't worry.

486
36:03.445 --> 36:06.771
Even though what happened wasn't caused by our course,

487
36:06.796 --> 36:08.703
we're still part of the same community.

488
36:08.728 --> 36:11.062
People from the community work here with us,

489
36:11.087 --> 36:13.390
and we rely on the community, too.

490
36:13.415 --> 36:15.784
My grandfather and father always told me

491
36:15.809 --> 36:17.442
that we're part of this community.

492
36:17.466 --> 36:19.206
We can't stand on our own.

493
36:19.230 --> 36:21.725
So Goodview Golf Club

494
36:21.750 --> 36:24.251
will work with the relevant authorities

495
36:24.276 --> 36:26.258
until everything returns to normal.

496
36:26.305 --> 36:29.016
And we'll cover all the expenses ourselves.

497
36:31.734 --> 36:34.285
Thank you. Thank you so much, Goodview Golf Club.

498
36:34.318 --> 36:36.222
- Thank you. - Thank you so much.

499
36:44.739 --> 36:49.250
We're sorry for the things we said to you earlier.

500
36:49.914 --> 36:52.683
If there's anything the community needs, please let us know.

501
36:52.708 --> 36:54.359
We're all on the same side.

502
37:09.486 --> 37:13.275
Looks like you won't be able to escape this course after all.

503
37:17.883 --> 37:19.927
Miss Nana, stop right there.

504
37:20.070 --> 37:22.070
Come with me. We've got a problem.

505
37:22.095 --> 37:23.460
What's wrong, Chef?

506
37:29.086 --> 37:31.543
Ton, what happened?

507
37:31.568 --> 37:34.264
Don't tell me you did something to Ton and then he...

508
37:34.289 --> 37:36.689
Hold on. I didn't do anything to him. Nothing inappropriate.

509
37:36.714 --> 37:38.811
He's handsome, sure, but I've already got my masseur.

510
37:38.836 --> 37:40.200
I wouldn't do something like that.

511
37:41.402 --> 37:44.619
Ton came to confess that he knows who's behind

512
37:44.644 --> 37:47.254
the smear campaign against our golf course.

513
37:48.407 --> 37:52.630
I was the one who took our course's food packaging

514
37:52.655 --> 37:55.995
and gave it to Mr. March at The Royal Green.

515
37:56.995 --> 37:59.304
You can punish me however you want.

516
37:59.329 --> 38:01.329
Just please don't fire me.

517
38:01.486 --> 38:03.688
I really had no choice, Miss.

518
38:03.713 --> 38:07.148
I... I really needed the money.

519
38:08.055 --> 38:09.726
You have no loyalty to this course.

520
38:09.751 --> 38:12.426
And were you the one who posted those lies about our course

521
38:12.450 --> 38:15.159
and my restaurant, too?

522
38:15.184 --> 38:16.866
You've caused me real damage, Ton.

523
38:16.891 --> 38:20.751
No, I didn't. But I know Mr. March's people did it.

524
38:20.909 --> 38:23.168
It was the people who left our course to work there.

525
38:23.193 --> 38:25.481
And as for the dead fish and that rotten smell,

526
38:25.506 --> 38:26.808
Mr. March was behind those, too.

527
38:27.831 --> 38:29.212
I knew it.

528
38:29.581 --> 38:32.177
That bastard March, that rotten relative!

529
38:33.505 --> 38:34.624
Are you calling me rotten?

530
38:35.952 --> 38:37.032
Ohhh... you mean March!

531
38:38.158 --> 38:41.430
Miss Nana, please calm down. I already questioned Ton.

532
38:41.582 --> 38:43.712
He had his reasons. He really needed the money.

533
38:43.737 --> 38:45.539
His younger brother is about to start school,

534
38:45.595 --> 38:47.570
and on top of that, his mother got sick.

535
38:50.642 --> 38:53.357
When we're talking money with someone who really needs it,

536
38:54.016 --> 38:55.762
I understand.

537
38:56.789 --> 38:58.226
I'm sorry, Miss Nana.

538
38:59.034 --> 39:00.054
It's okay.

539
39:00.395 --> 39:03.510
The root of the problem is the community's quality of life.

540
39:04.034 --> 39:06.488
When people are desperate for money,

541
39:06.702 --> 39:09.165
we end up letting money have power over us.

542
39:10.614 --> 39:12.473
I'm actually working on a scholarship program

543
39:12.498 --> 39:14.396
for kids in the community.

544
39:14.420 --> 39:17.071
Go talk to Belle. She'll tell you what you need to do.

545
39:17.096 --> 39:19.205
And when it comes to healthcare for the community,

546
39:19.230 --> 39:21.844
we'll arrange for a mobile medical unit to come here.

547
39:21.869 --> 39:24.437
We can use our course as a clinic once a month.

548
39:24.462 --> 39:25.971
Let's do it on our day off.

549
39:26.170 --> 39:27.796
Thank you so much, Miss Nana.

550
39:29.718 --> 39:33.429
And if you're ever in trouble again, come talk to us.

551
39:33.454 --> 39:36.410
I see everyone at this course as family.

552
39:36.561 --> 39:38.561
I won't tell anyone this time,

553
39:38.586 --> 39:40.456
but I'll put you on probation.

554
39:40.481 --> 39:43.425
If it happens again, I won't forgive you.

555
39:44.012 --> 39:45.020
Yes, Miss.

556
39:45.510 --> 39:47.026
Now go. Get back to work.

557
39:47.051 --> 39:49.581
Love this course the way it loves you, okay?

558
39:50.915 --> 39:52.323
Thank you, Miss Nana.

559
40:01.409 --> 40:05.526
Miss Nana, what are we gonna do about that Royal Green gang?

560
40:05.551 --> 40:06.675
We need to make them pay.

561
40:06.699 --> 40:09.170
You can't just go soft on them, Miss Nana.

562
40:09.670 --> 40:11.643
Chef, poop stinks.

563
40:11.668 --> 40:13.692
Then don't mess with it. Don't go near it.

564
40:13.717 --> 40:15.448
There's so much good stuff we can create here,

565
40:15.473 --> 40:17.408
so much positive energy to put into it.

566
40:17.433 --> 40:19.595
Let's not waste our time on things like this.

567
40:19.620 --> 40:20.885
I'm not letting them off.

568
40:20.909 --> 40:23.804
But I'd rather leave it to the authorities to deal with.

569
40:23.990 --> 40:28.548
Whoa! The light of virtue is shining right behind you!

570
40:28.573 --> 40:31.051
A saint has descended upon us! Everything's divine!

571
40:31.076 --> 40:34.643
Let me bow to you. Come on... whew!

572
40:43.439 --> 40:44.471
Nut.

573
40:47.011 --> 40:48.157
Have a seat.

574
40:50.685 --> 40:53.472
Do you think everything that's happened

575
40:53.497 --> 40:55.624
was the Royal Green's doing?

576
40:55.648 --> 40:56.766
It's possible.

577
40:57.030 --> 41:00.161
If they did it, what do they want?

578
41:00.303 --> 41:02.083
I knew Ms. Yupadee before.

579
41:05.114 --> 41:06.377
Very well.

580
41:07.138 --> 41:08.726
Did you two ever hook up?

581
41:10.083 --> 41:11.506
- Mm-hmm. - Ooh!

582
41:12.069 --> 41:13.651
I was just kidding.

583
41:16.919 --> 41:19.769
Ms. Yupadee is a ruthless businesswoman.

584
41:19.794 --> 41:21.853
She drives other businesses into the ground,

585
41:21.878 --> 41:25.068
then swoops in and offers to buy them for as little as possible.

586
41:26.951 --> 41:28.923
You call that helping?

587
41:28.948 --> 41:32.162
That's what she did to the hotel I used to work at in Chiang Rai.

588
41:32.190 --> 41:34.143
She used me as one of her pawns.

589
41:35.429 --> 41:38.162
So she wants our golf course?

590
41:38.383 --> 41:40.214
For as little as she can get it for.

591
41:40.618 --> 41:44.017
She'll run us into the ground until we're forced to sell.

592
41:44.815 --> 41:46.680
That's not very creative.

593
41:46.934 --> 41:51.125
She'll use her charm, her tricks, her money...

594
41:51.150 --> 41:54.526
anything she has to get what she wants,

595
41:54.551 --> 41:56.322
without caring who she hurts.

596
41:56.369 --> 42:00.055
If we're going up against her, you need to be very careful.

597
42:01.642 --> 42:03.934
I'll fight her with something she doesn't have.

598
42:05.458 --> 42:06.513
What's that?

599
42:08.010 --> 42:09.718
- Goodness. - Whoa.

600
42:11.244 --> 42:13.005
Don't laugh at me yet, Nut.

601
42:13.030 --> 42:14.565
I'm not being naive.

602
42:14.629 --> 42:18.646
I believe goodness, sincerity, and a positive attitude

603
42:18.671 --> 42:21.230
can help us find a way through almost any problem.

604
42:21.246 --> 42:22.762
Just look at what happened this time.

605
42:22.930 --> 42:24.956
Not only did they fail to frame us,

606
42:24.981 --> 42:27.512
they actually helped us regain the community's trust.

607
42:28.718 --> 42:31.464
Now that's a modern CEO.

608
42:31.489 --> 42:35.219
Guess you'll be back in France in less than six months, then.

609
42:40.094 --> 42:43.497
Oh, and what about the All Star Women's Golf Tournament?

610
42:43.947 --> 42:45.509
I've already worked out a plan.

611
42:45.534 --> 42:47.534
I'll present it at tomorrow's meeting.

612
42:47.777 --> 42:49.514
What about you, Nana?

613
42:49.539 --> 42:52.260
Have you decided who you'll nominate to represent our course?

614
42:52.356 --> 42:53.460
I have.

615
42:57.790 --> 43:02.183
Do you think Goodview will send you to represent the course?

616
43:02.809 --> 43:06.356
If they have to choose one, it'll probably be Pro Vee.

617
43:07.461 --> 43:08.795
I've followed the news.

618
43:09.570 --> 43:12.197
You almost won, but were penalized and lost.

619
43:13.085 --> 43:15.692
Two best friends had to face each other in the tournament...

620
43:15.717 --> 43:16.779
What do you want?

621
43:21.287 --> 43:22.596
Come back to our course.

622
43:23.159 --> 43:25.275
And I'll make sure you're the one who represents us.

623
43:26.610 --> 43:28.086
I believe

624
43:28.111 --> 43:31.079
a pro like you could beat Pro Vee any day.

625
43:31.378 --> 43:33.688
The pros from the other courses are nothing special.

626
43:34.450 --> 43:35.466
Don't you agree, Pro?

627
43:46.995 --> 43:50.737
Four months have already flown by since I took over the course.

628
43:50.762 --> 43:53.182
And business has been getting better and better.

629
43:53.207 --> 43:56.774
Who knows? We might even turn a profit this quarter.

630
43:56.799 --> 43:58.981
All thanks to this young CEO.

631
44:00.269 --> 44:02.203
Mr. Sanchai must be thrilled.

632
44:02.543 --> 44:06.069
And you might get to go back to France sooner than you expected.

633
44:06.951 --> 44:09.455
You deserves some credit, too.

634
44:10.140 --> 44:11.757
Mm. No, that's not right.

635
44:11.782 --> 44:16.247
Everyone at the course helped bring it back to life.

636
44:18.209 --> 44:20.657
You're quite capable, Nana. You know that?

637
44:21.899 --> 44:25.305
And your sincerity and straightforwardness

638
44:25.330 --> 44:27.330
have really won everyone over.

639
44:27.814 --> 44:30.133
Including you, right?

640
44:33.994 --> 44:36.752
Oh, there's one more thing. I was going to tell you then,

641
44:36.777 --> 44:38.390
but then all that happened.

642
44:38.415 --> 44:40.226
The Golf Course Network

643
44:40.251 --> 44:42.315
is organizing the All Star Women's Golf Tournament.

644
44:42.339 --> 44:45.422
Each course will send one golfer to represent them.

645
44:45.447 --> 44:47.645
The golfer from the winning course

646
44:47.670 --> 44:50.062
will earn the right to host the Asian Tour,

647
44:50.087 --> 44:52.379
which is a huge event at the end of the year.

648
44:52.698 --> 44:56.939
So I was thinking of sending you to represent Goodview.

649
44:57.803 --> 44:59.812
We have plenty of good pros here.

650
44:59.837 --> 45:01.058
Send someone else.

651
45:01.479 --> 45:04.273
No. It has to be you, Vee.

652
45:04.806 --> 45:06.811
I had Belle look into everyone.

653
45:06.836 --> 45:08.637
You're the best choice.

654
45:08.955 --> 45:10.422
I'd rather not compete.

655
45:10.883 --> 45:14.810
Why not? Please, Vee. Represent our course.

656
45:16.312 --> 45:17.351
No.

657
45:17.909 --> 45:19.657
I haven't competed in a long time.

658
45:19.682 --> 45:21.982
And I don't plan on competing again.

659
45:22.461 --> 45:23.517
Why not?

660
45:24.846 --> 45:26.776
There are some things I'd rather not explain.

661
45:29.402 --> 45:30.906
I'm not feeling well lately.

662
45:30.931 --> 45:33.719
I'll sleep in my room tonight.

663
45:33.744 --> 45:34.878
So you don't catch it.

664
46:09.570 --> 46:10.592
Can I shower with you?

665
46:13.032 --> 46:14.183
Sure.

666
49:05.129 --> 49:07.379
I'm moving back to the Royal Green.

667
49:12.968 --> 49:14.999
Have you gotten all the information you needed?

668
49:18.566 --> 49:21.967
You'd be disappointed in me if I did something like that.

669
49:22.509 --> 49:25.861
Not really. Everyone probably has their own reasons.

670
49:26.639 --> 49:28.308
But I'd be very disappointed

671
49:28.333 --> 49:30.593
if I were involved in something like this.

672
49:32.136 --> 49:33.794
So you're saying you didn't do it.

673
49:34.782 --> 49:36.743
Then why go back there?

674
49:37.314 --> 49:39.314
Because I want to matter for once.

675
49:40.106 --> 49:42.470
I want to prove myself.

676
49:42.495 --> 49:44.201
Prove I'm just as good as Pro Vee.

677
49:57.738 --> 49:58.767
- Hey. - Hmm?

678
49:58.792 --> 50:00.275
I brought you something today.

679
50:00.961 --> 50:02.770
- Let me guess. - Go ahead.

680
50:03.098 --> 50:05.129
- What is it? - Cake?

681
50:05.154 --> 50:07.330
- No way. Wrong. - Then let's just open it.

682
50:07.355 --> 50:08.782
- Go on. - Oh!

683
50:08.806 --> 50:10.240
Celadon from Chiang Mai.

684
50:10.265 --> 50:12.096
Whoa, pottery!

685
50:12.121 --> 50:13.161
Hey, look.

686
50:13.185 --> 50:14.427
Rub it three times and a genie pops out.

687
50:14.452 --> 50:16.653
- I know exactly what this is. - No, just put it away.

688
50:18.696 --> 50:20.910
- Thanks, buddy. Really, thanks. - Sure.

689
50:21.630 --> 50:23.533
Your daughter's really something.

690
50:23.558 --> 50:25.126
She's been doing all sorts of things.

691
50:25.150 --> 50:26.527
She's changed everything.

692
50:26.959 --> 50:29.507
Yeah, she really has. My wife and kids love it, too.

693
50:29.532 --> 50:32.198
They have so much to do while they're waiting for me.

694
50:32.262 --> 50:36.919
Look, you don't need to worry about your daughter's abilities.

695
50:36.943 --> 50:38.765
Just look at me. See?

696
50:38.789 --> 50:40.329
She's got it all from her old man.

697
50:40.354 --> 50:41.974
Yeah, that's true.

698
50:41.999 --> 50:46.578
Hey, have you told your kids yet about the cancer?

699
50:48.885 --> 50:50.687
Not yet. I don't have the heart to tell them.

700
50:50.712 --> 50:52.464
I'm afraid it'll only make things worse.

701
50:53.237 --> 50:55.495
I had her come back to help out

702
50:55.520 --> 50:57.264
so she'd get familiar with the business.

703
50:58.329 --> 51:00.332
If something happens to me someday,

704
51:01.168 --> 51:02.937
she'll be ready to take over.

705
51:02.962 --> 51:05.783
Come on. You're talking like you're about to die.

706
51:05.808 --> 51:08.293
There are so many ways to treat cancer nowadays.

707
51:08.318 --> 51:09.372
Don't be scared.

708
51:11.675 --> 51:16.412
I think you should start the chemo the doctor recommended.

709
51:16.624 --> 51:18.660
The sooner you start, the sooner you'll get better.

710
51:22.926 --> 51:24.603
I think I need a little more time.

711
51:25.365 --> 51:26.878
I just need some time to process it.

712
51:28.338 --> 51:30.743
Either way, you need to tell your kids.

713
51:31.354 --> 51:32.678
- Yeah, I agree. - Mm-hmm.

714
51:32.703 --> 51:35.203
- Here, eat. - Come on.

715
51:40.535 --> 51:43.846
Miss Nana, I had an urgent matter to take care of this morning.

716
51:43.871 --> 51:45.568
I'll come into the office this afternoon.

717
51:50.801 --> 51:52.221
You seem to be in a hurry.

718
51:54.375 --> 51:55.856
I guess it doesn't matter to anyone

719
51:55.881 --> 51:57.618
whether I'm here or not.

720
52:03.297 --> 52:05.378
You may not matter to some people,

721
52:05.982 --> 52:08.259
but that doesn't mean you don't matter to anyone.

722
52:10.058 --> 52:13.243
Me? Matter to someone?

723
52:13.997 --> 52:15.108
I doubt it.

724
52:18.705 --> 52:20.100
Don't say that.

725
52:21.188 --> 52:23.188
You're not just hurting yourself.

726
52:24.389 --> 52:28.025
You're also insulting the people who care about you.

727
52:31.912 --> 52:34.836
I'm off. I don't like goodbyes.

728
52:39.178 --> 52:40.968
I don't like them either.

729
52:44.427 --> 52:45.730
Then let's not say goodbye.

730
52:48.790 --> 52:49.893
No goodbyes.

731
52:50.566 --> 52:52.043
Just don't forget about us.

732
53:21.058 --> 53:22.772
Perfect, Nut. This is spot-on.

733
53:22.796 --> 53:24.951
Everyone's going to love our course.

734
53:26.059 --> 53:28.202
And have you decided who'll represent our course?

735
53:28.227 --> 53:29.710
Who did you choose, Nana?

736
53:30.296 --> 53:32.382
I'll make the final decision soon.

737
53:32.908 --> 53:34.122
Mm, sounds good.

738
53:34.289 --> 53:37.401
We also need to take profile photos of everyone competing.

739
53:37.950 --> 53:40.379
- Sure. - Okay. Thank you.

740
53:57.717 --> 54:01.607
Miss Nana, Pro Jin has notified HR that she's resigning.

741
54:03.329 --> 54:06.361
Why? Belle, what happened? Do you know?

742
54:10.987 --> 54:12.939
Pro Jin wants to represent a course

743
54:12.964 --> 54:15.471
in the upcoming All Star tournament.

744
54:15.662 --> 54:18.635
The Royal Green happened to offer her the opportunity,

745
54:18.897 --> 54:20.231
so she left.

746
54:22.586 --> 54:24.960
I didn't even think of that.

747
54:25.293 --> 54:28.138
If I were her, I'd probably feel hurt, too.

748
54:30.327 --> 54:33.278
And she wants to compete against Pro Vee

749
54:33.303 --> 54:36.080
to prove she's every bit as good as her.

750
54:37.934 --> 54:39.460
What do you mean, Belle?

751
54:39.485 --> 54:41.485
She believes Pro Vee cheated her.

752
54:43.278 --> 54:46.560
She was disqualified before the competition even ended.

753
54:48.218 --> 54:51.219
She believes that if she'd made it to the 18th hole,

754
54:51.244 --> 54:54.076
Pro Vee wouldn't have been the one to win that match.

755
54:55.248 --> 54:58.120
- Pro Vee cheated her? - Yes.

756
54:58.467 --> 55:00.737
Afterward, Pro Vee must've felt ashamed of a victory

757
55:00.762 --> 55:03.157
she'd cheated her way to.

758
55:03.193 --> 55:04.566
So she quit competing

759
55:04.591 --> 55:06.456
and became a golf instructor instead.

760
55:25.218 --> 55:26.535
Hello, Auntie.

761
55:28.273 --> 55:31.386
Nana! What brings you here, kid?

762
55:34.819 --> 55:38.600
What happened that day has stayed with Vee all this time.

763
55:39.993 --> 55:42.138
It was the final day of the tournament.

764
55:43.042 --> 55:44.200
Vee and Jin...

765
55:44.582 --> 55:46.706
had always trained together.

766
55:48.428 --> 55:50.659
Their scores had been neck and neck,

767
55:51.487 --> 55:53.792
but Jin was disqualified for breaking the rules.

768
55:54.562 --> 55:58.803
So Vee's score put her among the leaders,

769
56:00.234 --> 56:01.793
with a real shot at the title.

770
56:02.991 --> 56:06.930
But then her father had a heart attack.

771
56:08.297 --> 56:09.970
He had to be rushed to the hospital.

772
56:10.957 --> 56:15.458
At that point, Vee had only three holes left.

773
56:18.877 --> 56:22.044
We thought it wasn't anything too serious,

774
56:22.045 --> 56:23.846
so we told Vee to keep playing,

775
56:23.871 --> 56:25.785
while I rushed to the hospital.

776
56:26.571 --> 56:30.058
At first, Vee wasn't sure what to do.

777
56:30.657 --> 56:31.868
But in the end...

778
56:37.270 --> 56:39.533
she chose to stay and finish the game

779
56:39.558 --> 56:41.422
instead of going to her father.

780
56:49.526 --> 56:51.677
By the time Vee got to the hospital,

781
56:53.328 --> 56:54.685
it was too late.

782
56:57.523 --> 57:02.326
Her father was gone, and Vee never got to say goodbye.

783
57:05.884 --> 57:06.963
Vee...

784
58:00.192 --> 58:04.585
Her father was gone, and Vee never got to say goodbye.

785
58:08.383 --> 58:11.675
Vee blamed herself for choosing golf

786
58:11.700 --> 58:13.700
instead of going to her father.

787
58:15.657 --> 58:20.172
From then on, she never competed again.

788
58:24.097 --> 58:27.055
But Vee still plays golf.

789
58:29.077 --> 58:31.630
Vee loves golf.

790
58:32.746 --> 58:35.246
It was her only dream since she was a child.

791
58:38.427 --> 58:40.062
But after what happened,

792
58:41.181 --> 58:44.843
Vee turned away from competition

793
58:46.174 --> 58:51.570
and chose to stay in golf only as an instructor.

794
58:55.344 --> 58:56.460
And...

795
58:58.637 --> 59:00.637
What about Pro Jin's disqualification?

796
59:01.204 --> 59:03.021
Was it because of Vee's coach?

797
59:27.178 --> 59:28.185
Pro Vee.

798
59:31.260 --> 59:33.450
There's something I want to talk to you about.

799
59:33.929 --> 59:36.279
If this is about the All Star tournament,

800
59:36.304 --> 59:37.652
don't waste your time.

801
59:39.951 --> 59:41.723
I know everything now.

802
59:43.169 --> 59:45.676
About your father and the coach who...

803
59:45.701 --> 59:46.942
Who told you?

804
59:54.002 --> 59:55.349
That doesn't matter.

805
59:55.865 --> 59:59.303
What matters is that you're running away from it.

806
01:00:00.062 --> 01:00:01.750
You think I'm running away?

807
01:00:03.411 --> 01:00:04.498
Yes.

808
01:00:07.910 --> 01:00:11.649
Don't let your past dictate the path of your dreams.

809
01:00:12.824 --> 01:00:15.474
The coach I trusted made my friend

810
01:00:15.499 --> 01:00:17.892
leave the competition right before my eyes.

811
01:00:19.518 --> 01:00:21.870
And I didn't make it in time to say goodbye to my father

812
01:00:22.256 --> 01:00:24.073
because I chose to finish the game.

813
01:00:24.391 --> 01:00:26.369
How do you think I should feel

814
01:00:26.394 --> 01:00:28.761
about a victory I earned that way?

815
01:00:28.786 --> 01:00:30.972
So you never competed again

816
01:00:30.997 --> 01:00:32.686
because of what happened that day?

817
01:00:35.451 --> 01:00:38.034
That's exactly why I want you to compete.

818
01:00:38.485 --> 01:00:40.125
Everything that happened

819
01:00:40.150 --> 01:00:41.929
wasn't your fault.

820
01:00:41.954 --> 01:00:46.130
Don't let your whole life stop at that 18th hole, Vee.

821
01:00:46.155 --> 01:00:48.738
You want me to compete

822
01:00:48.763 --> 01:00:51.196
because you want our course to become famous again, right?

823
01:00:51.832 --> 01:00:55.257
You want everything to go perfectly, just like you planned.

824
01:00:56.865 --> 01:01:01.303
But my golfing career was never that beautiful.

825
01:01:02.222 --> 01:01:05.509
Everything fell apart the day I chose the trophy

826
01:01:05.534 --> 01:01:07.176
instead of my father.

827
01:01:15.284 --> 01:01:18.213
And now you're asking me to choose again.

828
01:01:19.573 --> 01:01:21.818
Between my pain

829
01:01:22.590 --> 01:01:24.298
and your success.

830
01:01:26.332 --> 01:01:27.898
And you should know

831
01:01:27.923 --> 01:01:29.174
what I'll choose.

832
01:01:34.922 --> 01:01:37.185
I'm not afraid to compete again.

833
01:01:38.973 --> 01:01:40.108
But I'm afraid that...

834
01:01:40.967 --> 01:01:46.089
this time, you'll be the one I have to lose.

835
01:01:46.220 --> 01:01:50.713
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

836
01:01:51.361 --> 01:01:56.427
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

837
01:01:56.452 --> 01:02:01.081
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

838
01:02:01.598 --> 01:02:06.347
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

839
01:02:07.009 --> 01:02:08.072
Pro Vee.

840
01:02:09.511 --> 01:02:12.218
Can I be honest with you about something?

841
01:02:12.385 --> 01:02:17.144
Nana never really had serious feelings for you.

842
01:02:17.169 --> 01:02:19.640
Dad, is there something you need to tell us?

843
01:02:19.665 --> 01:02:23.470
Oh, is it about the land I bought in Khao Yai? Or is it...

844
01:02:23.495 --> 01:02:24.970
About the cancer...

845
01:02:26.542 --> 01:02:28.652
Can I ask you something, Nana?

846
01:02:28.677 --> 01:02:29.834
What is it?

847
01:02:30.471 --> 01:02:32.433
Fahsai told me

848
01:02:32.458 --> 01:02:36.157
that the reason you've been so nice to me was to use me.

849
01:02:37.864 --> 01:02:42.385
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

850
01:02:42.907 --> 01:02:47.972
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

851
01:02:47.997 --> 01:02:53.188
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

852
01:02:53.213 --> 01:02:58.275
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

853
01:02:58.300 --> 01:03:03.419
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

854
01:03:03.444 --> 01:03:08.402
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

855
01:03:08.427 --> 01:03:11.604
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

856
01:03:11.629 --> 01:03:14.138
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

857
01:03:14.163 --> 01:03:19.711
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

858
01:03:19.737 --> 01:03:22.816
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

859
01:03:22.841 --> 01:03:27.691
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

860
01:03:28.932 --> 01:03:32.079
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

861
01:03:32.104 --> 01:03:34.718
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

862
01:03:34.742 --> 01:03:40.378
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

863
01:03:40.403 --> 01:03:43.606
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

864
01:03:43.631 --> 01:03:45.981
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

865
01:03:46.006 --> 01:03:49.716
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

866
01:03:51.748 --> 01:03:57.102
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

867
01:03:57.127 --> 01:04:02.141
♪ A thousand rounds, it'd still choose you ♪

868
01:04:02.166 --> 01:04:06.279
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪

869
01:04:06.279 --> 01:04:07.279
MkvDrama.net
